<title>UK: Courtaulds plans Singapore factory - report. [CORRECTED 07:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>Courtaulds plans Singapore factory - report. [CORRECTED 07:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Courtaulds Plc (corrects from Courtaulds Textiles Plc) is close to finalising plans to build a large plant in Singapore to produce its new Tencel fashion fabric, the Times newspaper said.</p>
<p>The Times said in its Monday edition that sales of Tencel garments at Britain's leading high-street retailer Marks &amp; Spencer Plc had outstripped forecasts and the fabric was crucial to Courtaulds' profit growth.</p>
<p>The report gave no financial details.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
